WEBVTT

NOTE
This file was generated by Descript <www.descript.com>

00:00:00.990 --> 00:00:04.210
BETH: Throughout life we are all
exposed to different life events

00:00:04.340 --> 00:00:05.900
and react to them in different ways.

00:00:06.370 --> 00:00:09.820
When autism is added into the
equation the problems are much

00:00:09.820 --> 00:00:11.250
greater for all concerned.

00:00:11.920 --> 00:00:15.109
Individuals with autism find
change and transition difficult

00:00:15.339 --> 00:00:16.859
and need that extra support.

00:00:17.369 --> 00:00:21.520
When those changes are life events that
affect the family dynamic, they can cause

00:00:21.560 --> 00:00:26.439
a great deal of upheaval, impacting on
the individual with autism by potentially

00:00:26.439 --> 00:00:30.449
destroying their routines and pulling
their safety net out from under them.

00:00:30.969 --> 00:00:34.890
JOE: The death of a family member can
have a devastating effect on everyone

00:00:34.890 --> 00:00:39.700
in the family, however, individuals with
autism react to death and experience

00:00:39.700 --> 00:00:41.300
the grieving process differently.

00:00:41.550 --> 00:00:45.790
They have difficulty connecting with their
emotions and may not cry, or they may show

00:00:45.790 --> 00:00:48.339
a delayed or extreme emotional response.

00:00:48.910 --> 00:00:52.069
They may potentially experience
an increase in their sensory

00:00:52.070 --> 00:00:56.580
sensitivities, meltdowns or shutdowns
and find it harder to organise,

00:00:56.730 --> 00:00:58.610
plan and concentrate on tasks.

00:00:58.920 --> 00:01:01.470
They may have difficulty
understanding how to behave in

00:01:01.470 --> 00:01:05.470
social situations such as funerals
and seeing other family members cry.

00:01:06.289 --> 00:01:09.750
BETH: The birth of a sibling may cause
a range of problems with individuals

00:01:09.750 --> 00:01:13.229
with autism such as finding it
difficult to ask questions about

00:01:13.270 --> 00:01:17.640
the pregnancy and birth process or
express their emotions about the birth.

00:01:18.260 --> 00:01:22.350
Having a new baby in the house can bring
its own problems, what will it be like?

00:01:22.789 --> 00:01:26.749
changes in rules and routines, or changes
in caregivers whilst their mother is

00:01:26.750 --> 00:01:28.739
in hospital or looking after the baby.

00:01:29.109 --> 00:01:32.589
They may struggle with sensory input
from the new sounds and smells a

00:01:32.590 --> 00:01:36.280
baby will bring and the behaviour
of the baby may confuse them.

00:01:36.810 --> 00:01:40.740
JOE: Major life changes will happen
with education, from starting nursery,

00:01:40.860 --> 00:01:45.070
through primary and secondary school
and maybe college and University, and on

00:01:45.080 --> 00:01:48.940
leaving school they need to be prepared
for work and for adulthood which can

00:01:48.990 --> 00:01:51.050
also bring some dramatic changes.

00:01:51.590 --> 00:01:54.100
BETH: Moving house can take them
from what they see as a secure

00:01:54.130 --> 00:01:58.600
place to somewhere that may have no
meaning to them, even though it may

00:01:58.600 --> 00:02:00.310
contain the same things and people.

00:02:00.880 --> 00:02:04.219
If the place they are moving to is
totally different, such as somewhere

00:02:04.219 --> 00:02:08.230
away from the family, where they may live
independently or with others with similar

00:02:08.320 --> 00:02:10.370
disorders they may struggle to settle.

00:02:10.770 --> 00:02:14.759
They may, however, find going off on
their own and making new relationships

00:02:14.760 --> 00:02:18.529
exciting, but this will possibly
challenging for others who have to

00:02:18.530 --> 00:02:20.240
support them through through the process.

00:02:21.030 --> 00:02:25.119
JOE: Minor or smaller transitions can
affect them such as changing class

00:02:25.119 --> 00:02:28.400
at the end of each year or moving
up a grade in a swimming class.

00:02:28.950 --> 00:02:32.760
Even daily transitions, moving
from one activity to another, from

00:02:32.760 --> 00:02:36.640
place to place, or person to person
can have a great impact on them.

00:02:37.420 --> 00:02:40.880
These ongoing transitions may not
seem like a major difficulty to

00:02:40.880 --> 00:02:44.420
others, but they can have a dramatic
effect on individuals with autism.

00:02:44.880 --> 00:02:48.400
BETH: The way such changes and
transitions are managed can make a big

00:02:48.450 --> 00:02:53.030
difference to an individual with autism’s
well-being, ability to learn skills,

00:02:53.300 --> 00:02:57.110
make progress and build relationships
in the future and possibly help

00:02:57.110 --> 00:02:59.449
with the more major changes in life.

